{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SuffixTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every suffix of every text ends at a leaf, the empty suffix included, and every internal node"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a point where suffixes that agree so far go different ways, so the tree has at most 2"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" + 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nodes. A pattern is found in O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") steps down from the root, and the leaves below where it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ends are its occurrences."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let tree = SuffixTree(\"banana\")","tree.occurrences(of: \"ana\").map(\\.range)   \/\/ [3 ..< 6, 1 ..< 4]","tree.longestRepeatedSubstring?.range       \/\/ 3 ..< 6, \"ana\"","","let both = SuffixTree(texts: [\"xabxac\", \"abcabxabcd\"])","both.longestCommonSubstring                \/\/ text 1, 3 ..< 7: \"abxa\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Nodes are numbered in preorder from the root at 0, so a node’s subtree is the nodes from it to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"just before the next node that is not its descendant. Children come in the order of the symbol","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that starts their edge: sorted when ","type":"text"},{"code":"Symbol","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the leaves are in the order of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their suffixes and match a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixArray","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" of the same text; otherwise in the order the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbols first occur in the texts. Each text ends in a terminator of its own that sorts before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every symbol and belongs to no label.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The tree converts to Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"RootedTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"RootedTree(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and its suffix links are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a directed graph, ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/suffixLinksView-swift.property","isActive":true},{"text":". Each node takes 32 bytes and each symbol 4 more, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"texts’ codes, which the tree keeps.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/suffixstructures\/suffixtree"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:16SuffixStructures0A4TreeV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SuffixTree"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"SuffixTree.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree.swift#L29"},"title":"SuffixTree","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SuffixTree"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"SuffixStructures"}]},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The suffix tree of one or more texts: the compressed trie of all their suffixes, built left to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"right in O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") (Ukkonen, “On-Line Construction of Suffix Trees”, 1995)."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures"]]},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/Occurrence","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/SuffixLinksView-swift.struct"]},{"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/init(texts:)"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/longestCommonSubstring","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/longestRepeatedSubstring","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/nodeCount","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/nodes","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStru